# User/tenant config — ship *.example instead, never real values
notify.conf
demo.conf.sh
repos.local.sh

# Credentials that live in HARNESS_DIR, which may be this checkout
linear-api-key

# Runtime state — never belongs in the repo. Anchored at the root: real run dirs
# only ever land here when HARNESS_DIR points at this checkout, and an unanchored
# `runs/` would also swallow the wall's committed fixtures (wall/fixtures/runs).
auth/
/runs/
.harness/

# The wall's city ledger. Unanchored on purpose: it lands beside whatever --runs
# points at, which includes wall/fixtures/ when somebody demos off the fixtures.
wall-city.jsonl
wall-city.jsonl.tmp

# Bought art packs. Licensed to the owner, not to this repository: the wall
# loads them off disk through the guarded /private/ route and not one byte of
# them may ever be committed. The README saying what goes there is the one
# tracked file, so the pattern ignores the CONTENTS rather than the directory —
# an ignored directory is never descended into and the negation below would
# never be reached.
wall/private/*
!wall/private/README.md

# Backups
*.bak*
AGENTS.md
